<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="A1.SS1.6" class="ltx_text">A-A</span> </span><span id="A1.SS1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof of Coverage Guarantees</span></h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To maintain formal coverage guarantees despite temporal dependencies, we follow the same proof style as in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite> and perform sequence-level calibration using the minimum score over phases.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.8" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof:</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let the calibration dataset be <span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i.i.d.</span> sequences of <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bar{x}^{n},\bar{y}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bar{x}^{n},\bar{y}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bar{x}^{\,n},\bar{y}^{\,n})\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\text{i.i.d.}}}{{\sim}}\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mover><mo>∼</mo><mtext>i.i.d.</mtext></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bar{x}^{\,n},\bar{y}^{\,n})\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\text{i.i.d.}}}{{\sim}}\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\text{calib}}=\{\{(x_{i}^{n},\mathcal{Y}_{i}^{n})\}_{i=0}^{M}\}_{n=1}^{N}=\{(\bar{x}^{\,n},\bar{y}^{\,n})\}_{n=1}^{N}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>calib</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{calib}}=\{\{(x_{i}^{n},\mathcal{Y}_{i}^{n})\}_{i=0}^{M}\}_{n=1}^{N}=\{(\bar{x}^{\,n},\bar{y}^{\,n})\}_{n=1}^{N},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{x}^{\,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{x}^{\,n}</annotation></semantics></math> is a sequence of query points and <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{y}^{\,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{y}^{\,n}</annotation></semantics></math> assigns to each
<math id="A1.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}^{n}\in\bar{x}^{\,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}^{n}\in\bar{x}^{\,n}</annotation></semantics></math> a set of correct labels <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}_{i}^{n}\subseteq\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}_{i}^{n}\subseteq\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For any sequence <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bar{x},\bar{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bar{x},\bar{y})</annotation></semantics></math>, define the per-point “multi-option” nonconformity score</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(x_{i},\mathcal{Y}_{i})\;:=\;1-\min_{y\in\mathcal{Y}_{i}}p^{\text{VLM}}(y\mid x_{i})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mtext>VLM</mtext></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(x_{i},\mathcal{Y}_{i})\;:=\;1-\min_{y\in\mathcal{Y}_{i}}p^{\text{VLM}}(y\mid x_{i}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">and define the sequence-level nonconformity score (equivalently to the theorem’s definition)</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa(\bar{x},\bar{y})\;:=\;1-\min_{x_{i}\in\bar{x}}\ \min_{y\in\mathcal{Y}_{i}}p^{\text{VLM}}(y\mid x_{i})\;=\;\max_{x_{i}\in\bar{x}}\,s(x_{i},\mathcal{Y}_{i})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mtext>VLM</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa(\bar{x},\bar{y})\;:=\;1-\min_{x_{i}\in\bar{x}}\ \min_{y\in\mathcal{Y}_{i}}p^{\text{VLM}}(y\mid x_{i})\;=\;\max_{x_{i}\in\bar{x}}\,s(x_{i},\mathcal{Y}_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa^{n}:=\kappa(\bar{x}^{\,n},\bar{y}^{\,n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa^{n}:=\kappa(\bar{x}^{\,n},\bar{y}^{\,n})</annotation></semantics></math> be the <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-th calibration score for
<math id="A1.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{q}</annotation></semantics></math> be the split-conformal quantile of
<math id="A1.SS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\kappa^{n}\}_{n=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\kappa^{n}\}_{n=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> at level <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. the
<math id="A1.SS1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lceil(N+1)(1-\varepsilon)\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lceil(N+1)(1-\varepsilon)\rceil</annotation></semantics></math>-th order statistic (standard split conformal rule).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 1: The standard conformal prediction guarantee for <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i.i.d." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i.i.d.</annotation></semantics></math> samples</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Draw an independent test sequence</p>
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bar{x}^{\,\text{test}},\bar{y}^{\,*})\sim\mathcal{D},\qquad\bar{x}^{\,\text{test}}=\{x_{i}^{\text{test}}\}_{i=0}^{M},\ \bar{y}^{\,*}=\{\mathcal{Y}_{i}^{*}\}_{i=0}^{M}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>test</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>test</mtext></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>test</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bar{x}^{\,\text{test}},\bar{y}^{\,*})\sim\mathcal{D},\qquad\bar{x}^{\,\text{test}}=\{x_{i}^{\text{test}}\}_{i=0}^{M},\ \bar{y}^{\,*}=\{\mathcal{Y}_{i}^{*}\}_{i=0}^{M},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and define its sequence-level score <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa^{\text{test}}:=\kappa(\bar{x}^{\,\text{test}},\bar{y}^{\,*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mtext>test</mtext></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>test</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa^{\text{test}}:=\kappa(\bar{x}^{\,\text{test}},\bar{y}^{\,*})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bar{x}^{\,1},\bar{y}^{\,1}),\dots,(\bar{x}^{\,N},\bar{y}^{\,N}),(\bar{x}^{\,\text{test}},\bar{y}^{\,*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn> 1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn> 1</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>test</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bar{x}^{\,1},\bar{y}^{\,1}),\dots,(\bar{x}^{\,N},\bar{y}^{\,N}),(\bar{x}^{\,\text{test}},\bar{y}^{\,*})</annotation></semantics></math>
are <span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i.i.d.</span> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa(\cdot,\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa(\cdot,\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is a deterministic function of a sequence,
the <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(N+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(N+1)</annotation></semantics></math> random variables <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\kappa^{1},\dots,\kappa^{N},\kappa^{\text{test}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mi>N</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mtext>test</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\kappa^{1},\dots,\kappa^{N},\kappa^{\text{test}})</annotation></semantics></math> are <span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i.i.d.</span>.
Hence, by the standard split conformal quantile guarantee,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr\!\left(\kappa^{\text{test}}\leq\hat{q}\right)\ \geq\ 1-\varepsilon." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.090em;" width="1.090em"><mi>Pr</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mtext>test</mtext></msup><mo>≤</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\!\left(\kappa^{\text{test}}\leq\hat{q}\right)\ \geq\ 1-\varepsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 2: Sequence-level calibration guarantees the per-point coverage as shown in Claim 1 in  <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite></h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Define the conformal prediction set for any query point <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> in any sequence by</p>
<table id="A1.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(x)\;:=\;\{y\in\mathcal{Y}:\ 1-p^{\text{VLM}}(y\mid x)\leq\hat{q}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mtext>VLM</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(x)\;:=\;\{y\in\mathcal{Y}:\ 1-p^{\text{VLM}}(y\mid x)\leq\hat{q}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">From Definition  <a href="#A1.Ex7" title="Proof: ‣ A-A Proof of Coverage Guarantees ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ When to Act, Ask, or Learn: Uncertainty-Aware Policy Steering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A-A</span></a>, we have <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa^{\text{test}}=\max_{x_{i}^{\text{test}}\in\bar{x}^{\,\text{test}}}s(x_{i}^{\text{test}},\mathcal{Y}_{i}^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mtext>test</mtext></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>test</mtext></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>test</mtext></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>test</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa^{\text{test}}=\max_{x_{i}^{\text{test}}\in\bar{x}^{\,\text{test}}}s(x_{i}^{\text{test}},\mathcal{Y}_{i}^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>
Since from Eq. <a href="#A1.Ex10" title="Step 1: The standard conformal prediction guarantee for 𝑖.𝑖.𝑑. samples ‣ A-A Proof of Coverage Guarantees ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ When to Act, Ask, or Learn: Uncertainty-Aware Policy Steering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A-A</span></a>, we have</p>
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr\!\left(\kappa^{\text{test}}\leq\hat{q}\right)\ \geq\ 1-\varepsilon." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.090em;" width="1.090em"><mi>Pr</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mtext>test</mtext></msup><mo>≤</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\!\left(\kappa^{\text{test}}\leq\hat{q}\right)\ \geq\ 1-\varepsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Then</p>
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr\!\left(\max_{x_{i}^{\text{test}}\in\bar{x}^{\,\text{test}}}s(x_{i}^{\text{test}},\mathcal{Y}_{i}^{*})\leq\hat{q}\right)\ \geq\ 1-\varepsilon." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.090em;" width="1.090em"><mi>Pr</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>test</mtext></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>test</mtext></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>test</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\!\left(\max_{x_{i}^{\text{test}}\in\bar{x}^{\,\text{test}}}s(x_{i}^{\text{test}},\mathcal{Y}_{i}^{*})\leq\hat{q}\right)\ \geq\ 1-\varepsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Given that</p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall x^{\text{test}}\in\bar{x}^{\text{test}},s(x^{\text{test}},\mathcal{Y}_{i}^{*})\leq\max_{x_{i}^{\text{test}}\in\bar{x}^{\,\text{test}}}s(x_{i}^{\text{test}},\mathcal{Y}_{i}^{*})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mtext>test</mtext></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>test</mtext></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mtext>test</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>test</mtext></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>test</mtext></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>test</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall x^{\text{test}}\in\bar{x}^{\text{test}},s(x^{\text{test}},\mathcal{Y}_{i}^{*})\leq\max_{x_{i}^{\text{test}}\in\bar{x}^{\,\text{test}}}s(x_{i}^{\text{test}},\mathcal{Y}_{i}^{*})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">We have</p>
<table id="A1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall x^{\text{test}}\in\bar{x}^{\text{test}},\Pr\!\left(s(x_{i}^{\text{test}},\mathcal{Y}_{i}^{*})\leq\hat{q}\right)\ \geq\ 1-\varepsilon" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mtext>test</mtext></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>test</mtext></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.090em;" width="1.090em"><mi>Pr</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>test</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall x^{\text{test}}\in\bar{x}^{\text{test}},\Pr\!\left(s(x_{i}^{\text{test}},\mathcal{Y}_{i}^{*})\leq\hat{q}\right)\ \geq\ 1-\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.6" class="ltx_p">This indicates if the test sequence <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{x}^{\text{test}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>test</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{x}^{\text{test}}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the guarantee, then any query point <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\text{test}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mtext>test</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\text{test}}</annotation></semantics></math> in the test sequence also satisfies the guarantee.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 3: Minimum score over true option sets guarantees all true options are included</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">From Definition <a href="#A1.Ex5" title="Proof: ‣ A-A Proof of Coverage Guarantees ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ When to Act, Ask, or Learn: Uncertainty-Aware Policy Steering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A-A</span></a> and Eq. <a href="#A1.Ex17" title="Step 2: Sequence-level calibration guarantees the per-point coverage as shown in Claim 1 in [] ‣ A-A Proof of Coverage Guarantees ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ When to Act, Ask, or Learn: Uncertainty-Aware Policy Steering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A-A</span></a>, we know <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall x^{\text{test}}\in\bar{x}^{\text{test}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mtext>test</mtext></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mtext>test</mtext></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall x^{\text{test}}\in\bar{x}^{\text{test}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr\!\left(1-\min_{y\in\mathcal{Y}^{*}}p^{\text{VLM}}(y\mid x_{i}^{\text{test}})\leq\hat{q}\right)\ \geq\ 1-\varepsilon" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.090em;" width="1.090em"><mi>Pr</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mtext>VLM</mtext></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>test</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\!\left(1-\min_{y\in\mathcal{Y}^{*}}p^{\text{VLM}}(y\mid x_{i}^{\text{test}})\leq\hat{q}\right)\ \geq\ 1-\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Given that</p>
<table id="A1.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall y^{\prime}\in\mathcal{Y}_{i}^{*},1-p^{\text{VLM}}(y^{\prime}\mid x_{i}^{\text{test}})\leq 1-\min_{y\in\mathcal{Y}_{i}^{*}}p^{\text{VLM}}(y\mid x_{i}^{\text{test}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mtext>VLM</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>test</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mtext>VLM</mtext></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>test</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall y^{\prime}\in\mathcal{Y}_{i}^{*},1-p^{\text{VLM}}(y^{\prime}\mid x_{i}^{\text{test}})\leq 1-\min_{y\in\mathcal{Y}_{i}^{*}}p^{\text{VLM}}(y\mid x_{i}^{\text{test}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">We have <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall y^{\prime}\in\mathcal{Y}_{i}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall y^{\prime}\in\mathcal{Y}_{i}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr\!\left(1-p^{\text{VLM}}(y^{\prime}\mid x_{i}^{\text{test}})\leq 1-\min_{y\in\mathcal{Y}_{i}^{*}}p^{\text{VLM}}(y\mid x_{i}^{\text{test}})\leq\hat{q}\right)\geq 1-\varepsilon" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.090em;" width="1.090em"><mi>Pr</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mtext>VLM</mtext></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>test</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mtext>VLM</mtext></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>test</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\!\left(1-p^{\text{VLM}}(y^{\prime}\mid x_{i}^{\text{test}})\leq 1-\min_{y\in\mathcal{Y}_{i}^{*}}p^{\text{VLM}}(y\mid x_{i}^{\text{test}})\leq\hat{q}\right)\geq 1-\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, combined with Definition <a href="#A1.Ex12" title="Step 2: Sequence-level calibration guarantees the per-point coverage as shown in Claim 1 in [] ‣ A-A Proof of Coverage Guarantees ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ When to Act, Ask, or Learn: Uncertainty-Aware Policy Steering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A-A</span></a>, we get</p>
<table id="A1.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr\!\big(\mathcal{Y}_{i}^{*}\subseteq C(x_{i}^{\text{test}})\big)\ \geq\ 1-\varepsilon," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.090em;" width="1.090em"><mi>Pr</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>test</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\!\big(\mathcal{Y}_{i}^{*}\subseteq C(x_{i}^{\text{test}})\big)\ \geq\ 1-\varepsilon,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">which proves the claim.
∎We have proved that <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr\!\big(\mathcal{Y}_{i}^{*}\subseteq C(x_{i}^{\text{test}})\big)\geq 1-\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.090em;" width="1.090em"><mi>Pr</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>test</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\!\big(\mathcal{Y}_{i}^{*}\subseteq C(x_{i}^{\text{test}})\big)\geq 1-\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, where the probability is taken over the random draw from the calibration set <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\text{calib}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>calib</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{calib}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the test pair <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(x_{i}^{\text{test}},\mathcal{Y}^{*}_{i}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>test</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(x_{i}^{\text{test}},\mathcal{Y}^{*}_{i}\big)</annotation></semantics></math>; that is, the result is a marginal coverage guarantee. Consequently, achieving the target coverage for each new test point would, in principle, require a freshly sampled calibration set. However, following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite>, we use the dataset-conditional guarantee
— conditioning on the realized calibration dataset — which can be applied to new test samples without re-calibration.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="A1.SS2.6" class="ltx_text">A-B</span> </span><span id="A1.SS2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Aside on our score function design</span></h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Prior work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite>
uses the <span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">max</span> score to get an existence guarantee in Eq <a href="#A1.E6" title="In A-B Aside on our score function design ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ When to Act, Ask, or Learn: Uncertainty-Aware Policy Steering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> and is designed to ensure the prediction set contains <em id="A1.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">at least one</em> acceptable choice and then commits to a single selected option.
We aim to include <em id="A1.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">all</em> suitable options in the prediction set by using a more conservative score that minimizes over options to achieve a completeness guarantee (Eq. <a href="#A1.E7" title="In A-B Aside on our score function design ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ When to Act, Ask, or Learn: Uncertainty-Aware Policy Steering" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>). From a user perspective, this avoids guessing the user’s unstated intent and instead displays the set of plausible choices for quick disambiguation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
